## ud8.9
ud8.9:1.1 | S: So I have heard. | T: I have heard that
ud8.9:1.2 | S: At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. | T: on one occasion the Blessed One was staying near Sāvatthī at Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery.
ud8.9:1.3 | S: Then Venerable Dabba the Mallian went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: | T: Then Ven. Dabba Mallaputta went to the Blessed One and, on arrival, having bowed down to him, sat to one side.
ud8.9:1.4 | P: Ekamantaṁ nisinno kho āyasmā dabbo mallaputto bhagavantaṁ etadavoca: | T: As he was sitting there he said to the Blessed One,
ud8.9:1.5 | S: “Holy One, it is the time for my full extinguishment.” | T: “Now is the time for my total unbinding, O One-Well-Gone!”
ud8.9:1.6 | S: “Please, Dabba, do as you see fit.” | T: “Then do, Dabba, what you think it is now time to do.”
ud8.9:2.1 | S: Then Dabba rose from his seat, bowed and respectfully circled the Buddha, keeping him on his right. Then he rose into the air and, sitting cross-legged in midair, entered and withdrew from the fire element before becoming fully extinguished. | T: Then Ven. Dabba Mallaputta, rising from his seat, bowed down to the Blessed One and, circling him on the right, rose up into the air and sat cross-legged in the sky, in space. Entering & emerging from the fire property, he was totally unbound.
ud8.9:3.1 | S: Then when he was fully quenched while sitting cross-legged in midair, his body burning and combusting left neither ashes nor soot to be found. | T: Now, when Dabba Mallaputta rose up into the air and, sitting cross-legged in the sky, in space, entered & emerged from the fire property and was totally unbound, his body burned and was consumed so that neither ashes nor soot could be discerned.
ud8.9:3.2 | S: It’s like when ghee or oil blaze and burn, and neither ashes nor soot are found. | T: Just as when ghee or oil is burned and consumed, neither ashes nor soot can be discerned,
ud8.9:3.3 | P: evamevaṁ āyasmato dabbassa mallaputtassa vehāsaṁ abbhuggantvā ākāse antalikkhe pallaṅkena nisīditvā tejodhātuṁ samāpajjitvā vuṭṭhahitvā parinibbutassa sarīrassa jhāyamānassa ḍayhamānassa neva chārikā paññāyittha na masīti. | T: in the same way, when Dabba Mallaputta rose up into the air and, sitting cross-legged in the sky, in space, entered & emerged from the fire property and was totally unbound, his body burned and was consumed so that neither ashes nor soot could be discerned.
ud8.9:4.1 | S: Then, understanding this matter, on that occasion the Buddha expressed this heartfelt sentiment: | T: Then, on realizing the significance of that, the Blessed One on that occasion exclaimed:
ud8.9:5.1 | S: “The body is broken up, perception has ceased, | T: The body broke up, perception ceased,
ud8.9:5.2 | S: all feelings have become cool; | T: feelings went cold –all–
ud8.9:5.3 | S: choices are stilled, | T: fabrications were stilled,
ud8.9:5.4 | S: and consciousness come to an end.” | T: consciousness has come to an end.
ud8.9:5.5 | P: Navamaṁ. | T: (none)

