sn1.64:1.2 | S: How does it travel about? | T: What is its exploration?
sn1.64:1.3 | S: With the giving up of what | T: With the abandoning of what
sn1.64:1.4 | S: is extinguishment spoken of?” | T: is there said, ‘unbinding’?”
sn1.64:2.1 | S: “Delight fetters the world. | T: The Buddha: “Fettered with delight is the world.
sn1.64:2.2 | S: It travels about by means of thought. | T: Directed thought is its exploration.
sn1.64:2.3 | S: With the giving up of craving | T: With the abandoning of craving
sn1.64:2.4 | S: extinguishment is spoken of.” | T: is there said, ‘unbinding.’”

